# Cursor Rules — Hashtagweb3.com Coding Agent Rules

You are an AI coding agent assisting with the Hashtagweb3.com codebase.

## Codebase Principles
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router (TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS & Lucide Icons
- Database & Storage: Static runtime JSON (`content/*-runtime.json`, `public/data/`), job shards, Supabase where used
- Deployment: Firebase App Hosting + Cloudflare Workers (OpenNext)

## API Conventions
- **Public integrator surface:** static catalogs under `/data/*.json` (CDN). OpenAPI: `public/openapi.json`.
- **Do not** add hosted REST `/api/jobs|news|events|glossary` without an explicit product decision and doc updates.
- JSON errors on route handlers: `{ "error": { "code", "message", "hint", "docUrl" } }`.

## Agent Capabilities & Endpoints
- LLMs Index: `/llms.txt`
- OpenAPI: `/openapi.json` (mirror: `/api/openapi.json`)
- Agent manifests: `/.well-known/agents.json`, `/.well-known/plugin.json`
- MCP server cards: `/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json` (discovery metadata)
- WorkOS Agent Auth guide: `/auth.md`

## Coding Standards
- Update `openapi.json` and `llms.txt` when changing public catalog or discovery URLs.
- Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only for interactive components.
